    <string name="no_how_it_works_title">How does \"NO\" work?</string>
    <string name="no_how_it_works_body">1) Block: Standard blocking words are active by default. You can disable any word or add your own.
2) Focus Mode: For special moments like meetings, it blocks all notifications — including those you usually allow — and saves them inside the app.
3) App Exemption: No notification from the selected app is ever blocked; it appears normally.
4) Emoji Block: Blocks all notifications that contain emojis. For apps where you do not want emoji notifications blocked, use the Allow emojis option in the app detail.
5) Archive: Keeps your notification history for the last 7 days.
6) Allow Words: Notifications containing the words you add here will never be blocked.
7) Sign in with Google: Used to protect your notification history even if you clear cookies or reinstall the app. Signing in with Google is optional.</string>

